% Marketplace listings read for the tariff, with the customs background
% (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §6; language reference §14.5).
%
% A shop listing does not speak the words of the tariff. This file names the
% facts background that "Write it in English" uses to read a listing: the
% listing's fields, the words for garments and fabrics, the names of
% materials (bridges, each from a public text); the customs presumptions
% (from US Customs' publications and rulings); and trade usage (the rules
% no text supports, stated by the authors). The tariff never reasons with
% the background: it reads the facts that come out of it, each with its
% origin.
%
% Three readings of a case (§17.5): the listing reading admits the listing
% and the bridges; the presumed reading adds the customs presumptions; the
% usage reading adds trade usage.

the target language is: prolog.

the facts background includes these resources:
    background/listings, background/garments, background/articles, background/uses, background/materials,
    background/jewellery, background/footwear, background/trade_usage, background/presumptions.

the templates are:
    *a good* is classified in *a code* by *a reading*.

the knowledge base marketplace includes these resources:
    tariff.

the knowledge base marketplace includes:

a good is classified in a code by a reading
    if the reading is in [listing reading, presumed reading, usage reading]
    and the subheading of the good is the code
        according to the reading.

the listing is admissible under listing reading.
the listing is admissible under presumed reading.
the listing is admissible under usage reading.
marketplace listings is admissible under listing reading.
marketplace listings is admissible under presumed reading.
marketplace listings is admissible under usage reading.
garments background is admissible under listing reading.
garments background is admissible under presumed reading.
garments background is admissible under usage reading.
jewellery background is admissible under listing reading.
jewellery background is admissible under presumed reading.
jewellery background is admissible under usage reading.
footwear background is admissible under listing reading.
footwear background is admissible under presumed reading.
footwear background is admissible under usage reading.
materials background is admissible under listing reading.
materials background is admissible under presumed reading.
materials background is admissible under usage reading.
uses background is admissible under presumed reading.
uses background is admissible under usage reading.
customs presumptions is admissible under presumed reading.
customs presumptions is admissible under usage reading.
trade usage is admissible under usage reading.

% A men's T-shirt as a listing describes it ("Men Tee Shirt", "Material:
% Cotton", "Craft of Weaving: Knit"), read with the background: the T-shirt's
% fabric is presumed, so only the presumed reading gives a code.
scenario tee is, as stated in the listing:
    tee is classified under the US tariff.
    the cut of tee indicates men, confer "Gender: Men".
    tee contains 100 percent of cotton, confer "Material: Cotton".
    the fabric construction of tee is knitted, according to marketplace listings, because "craft_of_weaving_field", confer "Craft of Weaving: Knit".
    the kind of tee is T-shirt, according to garments background, because "kind_by_name", confer "Men T-shirt".
    tee is a manufactured article, according to marketplace listings, because "finished_product", confer "Men T-shirt".
    the fabric of tee is lightweight, according to customs presumptions, because "tshirt_fabric", confer "Men T-shirt".
    tee is of plain knit fabric, according to customs presumptions, because "tshirt_plain_knit", confer "Men T-shirt".
    readings expects answers ["tee is classified in 6109.10 by presumed reading", "tee is classified in 6109.10 by usage reading"].

% The same T-shirt with nothing presumed: the rules ask for the fabric
% instead of falling through to the sweaters of heading 6110.
scenario tee_unread is, as stated in the listing:
    tee is classified under the US tariff.
    the cut of tee indicates men.
    tee contains 100 percent of cotton.
    the fabric construction of tee is knitted.
    the kind of tee is T-shirt.
    tee is a manufactured article.
    subheadings expects answers [].

% A dress of "POLYESTER, Spandex" with no shares: trade usage presumes that
% the first fibre named predominates.
scenario dress is, as stated in the listing:
    dress is classified under the US tariff.
    the cut of dress indicates women, confer "Gender: Women".
    the kind of dress is dress, confer "Item Type: Prom Dresses".
    dress is a manufactured article, according to marketplace listings, because "finished_product", confer "Item Type: Prom Dresses".
    the fabric construction of dress is woven, confer "woven".
    the material that predominates by weight in dress is polyester, according to trade usage, because "first_named_predominates", confer "Material: POLYESTER,Spandex".
    readings expects answers ["dress is classified in 6204.43 by usage reading"].

% A bracelet as a listing describes it ("Item Type: BRACELETS", "Metals
% Type: Zinc Alloy", "Main Stone: cubic zirconia"), read with the jewellery
% background: a cubic zirconia is a stone of Chapter 71 (US Customs, HQ
% H328582), so the bracelet is no imitation jewelry but an article of stones.
scenario bracelet is, as stated in the listing:
    bracelet is classified under the US tariff.
    the kind of bracelet is bracelet, according to jewellery background, because "jewellery_kind_by_field", confer "Item Type: BRACELETS".
    bracelet is a manufactured article, according to marketplace listings, because "finished_product_field", confer "Item Type: BRACELETS".
    the metal of bracelet is zinc alloy, according to jewellery background, because "metal_by_field", confer "Metals Type: Zinc Alloy".
    the gem of bracelet is cubic zirconia, according to jewellery background, because "gem_by_field", confer "Main Stone: cubic zirconia".
    readings expects answers ["bracelet is classified in 7116.20 by listing reading", "bracelet is classified in 7116.20 by presumed reading", "bracelet is classified in 7116.20 by usage reading"].

% The same bracelet with no stone, of plastics: imitation jewelry (Chapter
% 39 note 2(r) takes it out of heading 3926)
scenario plastic_bracelet is, as stated in the listing:
    plastic bracelet is classified under the US tariff.
    the kind of plastic bracelet is bracelet, according to jewellery background, because "jewellery_kind_by_field", confer "Item Type: BRACELETS".
    plastic bracelet is a manufactured article, according to marketplace listings, because "finished_product_field", confer "Item Type: BRACELETS".
    plastic bracelet is made of plastics, according to materials background, because "plastics_by_name", confer "Material: Plastic".
    readings expects answers ["plastic bracelet is classified in 7117.90 by listing reading", "plastic bracelet is classified in 7117.90 by presumed reading", "plastic bracelet is classified in 7117.90 by usage reading"].

% A lace front wig of human hair ("Lace Wig Type: Lace Front Wigs", "Human
% Hair Type: Brazilian Hair")
scenario lace_wig is, as stated in the listing:
    the lace wig is classified under the US tariff.
    the kind of the lace wig is wig, according to jewellery background, because "jewellery_kind_by_type_field", confer "Lace Wig Type: Lace Front Wigs".
    the lace wig is a manufactured article, according to marketplace listings, because "finished_product_field", confer "Lace Wig Type: Lace Front Wigs".
    the hair of the lace wig is human hair, according to jewellery background, because "hair_by_human_hair_field", confer "Human Hair Type: Brazilian Hair".
    readings expects answers ["the lace wig is classified in 6704.20 by listing reading", "the lace wig is classified in 6704.20 by presumed reading", "the lace wig is classified in 6704.20 by usage reading"].

% A boot as a listing describes it ("Item Type: BOOTS", "Upper Material:
% PU", "Outsole Material: Rubber", "Upper coverage: Above the ankle but not
% to the knee"), read with the footwear background: other footwear of
% rubber or plastics covering the ankle (Chapter 39 note 2(q) takes it out
% of heading 3926).
scenario boots is, as stated in the listing:
    the boots is classified under the US tariff.
    the kind of the boots is boot, according to footwear background, because "footwear_kind_by_field", confer "Item Type: BOOTS".
    the boots is a manufactured article, according to marketplace listings, because "finished_product_field", confer "Item Type: BOOTS".
    the constituent material of the upper of the boots is polyurethane, according to footwear background, because "upper_material_field", confer "Upper Material: PU".
    the constituent material of the outer sole of the boots is rubber, according to footwear background, because "outsole_material_field", confer "Outsole Material: Rubber".
    the boots covers the ankle, according to footwear background, because "coverage_ankle", confer "Upper coverage: Above the ankle but not to the knee".
    readings expects answers ["the boots is classified in 6402.91 by listing reading", "the boots is classified in 6402.91 by presumed reading", "the boots is classified in 6402.91 by usage reading"].

% A shoulder bag of PU ("Handbags Type: Shoulder Bags", "Main Material:
% PU"): a handbag with an outer surface of sheeting of plastics (Chapter 39
% note 2(m) takes it out of heading 3926)
scenario shoulder_bag is, as stated in the listing:
    the shoulder bag is classified under the US tariff.
    the kind of the shoulder bag is handbag, according to footwear background, because "footwear_kind_by_field", confer "Handbags Type: Shoulder Bags".
    the shoulder bag is a manufactured article, according to marketplace listings, because "finished_product_field", confer "Handbags Type: Shoulder Bags".
    the outer surface of the shoulder bag is of sheeting of plastics, according to footwear background, because "bag_material_field", confer "Main Material: PU".
    the shoulder bag is wholly or mainly of sheeting of plastics, according to footwear background, because "main_material_field", confer "Main Material: PU".
    readings expects answers ["the shoulder bag is classified in 4202.22 by listing reading", "the shoulder bag is classified in 4202.22 by presumed reading", "the shoulder bag is classified in 4202.22 by usage reading"].

query readings is:
    which good is classified in which code by which reading.

query subheadings is:
    the subheading of which good is which code.
